- B | leave the family lunch early to meet the people who can help your career | act: leave the family lunch early to meet the people who can help their career | v: achievement, power | sphere: learn.B | chance: 65
- R | skip the smart lunch, and take the whole family for a loud meal you cannot afford | act: skip the smart lunch, and take the whole family for a loud meal they cannot afford | v: hedonism, benevolence | sphere: learn.R | chance: 65
- G | hang the certificate in your parents' front room, where the whole street will see it | act: hang the certificate in their parents' front room, where the whole street will see it | v: tradition, security | sphere: learn.G | chance: 65
- BR | take the best-paid offer in the city that same week, and send money home | v: achievement, stimulation | mark: moved away | sphere: learn.BR | chance: 55
- RG | throw a party on the home street, and invite every neighbour who ever helped | v: tradition, hedonism | sphere: learn.RG | chance: 55
- UG | ask the grandparents for the story of why none of them could study | v: tradition, universalism | sphere: learn.GU | chance: 55
- WB | set up a small fund so the next cousin can study without your debts | act: set up a small fund so the next cousin can study without their debts | v: benevolence, achievement | lever: fund | sphere: learn.WB | chance: 55
- WU | go back to your old school, and tell the pupils there that it can be done | act: go back to their old school, and tell the pupils there that it can be done | v: universalism, benevolence | sphere: learn.WU | chance: 55
works: The photo from that day goes up on {Ns} parents' wall, and stays there for the rest of their lives.
works: Two years later a younger cousin applies to the same college, and names {N} as the reason.
fails: The family feels out of place all day, and the drive home is quiet and stiff.
fails: The certificate opens fewer doors than promised, and {N} goes back to the same job as before, with a debt.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: the day the old knowledge proves right (pairs D2a)

== the old well that never ran dry
tier: life event
sphere: learn
ladder: known
stages: adult mature elder
age: 40-95
per_year: 0 0 0 .002 .005 .008
drivers: harsh+.3 community+.2 era-.1
times: Local knowledge that experts first dismissed and later relied on (springs, weather signs, flood lines, old ways of building) is well known (estimate; Berkes 2012 on traditional ecological knowledge); a time when what the elders taught is proved right in front of the town comes to about 1 in 5 lives, mostly after 45
likelier: a person who grew up in the same town, a grandparent who taught the land, a dry or hard year, a small place
rarer: a newcomer to the town, a big city, a family that moved often, a person who never listened to the old ones
gap: 10-40
tone: joy
life: community, neighbours, family
horizon: months
roles: neighbour, friend, child
who: neighbour
earth: in the long drought the taps run two hours a day, and the old well your grandfather showed you, the one the engineers called dry, still runs
scene: The drought is in its third month, and the taps in {place} run for two hours a day. {N} remembers the old well behind the chapel that {Ns} grandfather once showed them. The engineers said years ago it was dry. It is not.
scene W: Water in {place} belongs to everyone, and {N} wants it shared fairly, by a list, before anyone else gets ideas.
scene U: {N} wants to know why the engineers' maps missed it, and what else the old ones knew that nobody wrote down.
scene B: Whoever holds the key to that well this summer will be owed something by half the town.
scene R: {N} has already been down with a bucket and a torch, and came up soaked to the knees and laughing.
scene G: {Ns} grandfather said the spring never fails while it is kept clean. He said it every summer, and nobody listened.
- W | tell the council at once, and ask for a fair rota at the well | v: universalism, conformity | lever: voice | pushes: place | sphere: learn.W | chance: 65
- U | bring the engineers to see it, and find out why their maps missed it | v: universalism, self-direction | sphere: learn.U | chance: 65
- B | keep the key yourself, and decide who draws water from the well | act: keep the key themselves, and decide who draws water from the well | v: power | sphere: learn.B | chance: 65
- R | clear the well out yourself this weekend, with whoever turns up to help | act: clear the well out themselves this weekend, with whoever turns up to help | v: stimulation, benevolence | sphere: learn.R | chance: 65
- G | clean the spring the old way, and say your grandfather's words over it | act: clean the spring the old way, and say their grandfather's words over it | v: tradition | sphere: learn.G | chance: 65
- BG | have the council name the well after your family before you hand it over | act: have the council name the well after their family before they hand it over | v: tradition, power | sphere: learn.BG | chance: 55
- BR | stand up at the town meeting, and tell the engineers to their faces they were wrong | v: power, stimulation | lever: voice | sphere: learn.BR | chance: 55
- UR | test the water with a kit from the shop, and post the results for the town | v: universalism, stimulation | sphere: learn.UR | chance: 55
- WG | teach the children at the school how to find and keep a spring | v: tradition, benevolence | sphere: learn.GW | chance: 55
- WU | write down all the old ones said about water, and give it to the library | v: universalism, tradition | sphere: learn.WU | chance: 55
works: The well carries the street through to the autumn rains, and the council puts the old spring on its maps.
works: For the rest of the summer people stop {N} in the market to ask what else the old ones knew.
fails: The council fences the well off as unsafe, and the engineers take the credit when it opens again.
fails: The water turns out fit only for gardens, and half the town laughs at the fuss {N} made.
